  "knowledge": "Cabin Habitability Standard",
  "description": "Defines the minimum standards for habitable cabin conditions in polar environments.",
  "definition": "A cabin meets 'Habitability Standards' when it maintains internal temperature (cabinclimate.temperature_c) between 18-24\u00b0C, oxygen levels (cabinclimate.o2_percent) above 19.5%, CO2 levels (cabinclimate.co2_ppm) below 1000 ppm, functioning ventilation systems, and operational heating systems."
}

{
